# carval API — cookie-session auth + reports
# Flow: signup/signin set a session cookie (cookie-session); whoami reads it.
# Note: signout only nulls session.userId — it does NOT clear the cookie.

### 1. Sign up — creates user + sets session cookie (admin defaults to true)
POST http://localhost:3000/auth/signup
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "d.darshana@test.com",
  "password": "1qaz!QAZ"
}

### 2. Sign in — validates credentials + sets session cookie
POST http://localhost:3000/auth/signin
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "d.darshana@test.com",
  "password": "1qaz!QAZ"
}

### 3. Get user by id — 404 if not found
GET http://localhost:3000/auth/3

### 4. Find users by email — note: intentionally unguarded
GET http://localhost:3000/auth?email=d.darshana@newpath.com

### 5. Delete user by id — intentionally unguarded
DELETE http://localhost:3000/auth/2

### 6. Update user by id (email only) — intentionally unguarded
PATCH http://localhost:3000/auth/2
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "d.darshana@newpath.com"
}

### 7. Who am I — requires session cookie (AuthGuard) -> 401 if signed out
GET http://localhost:3000/auth/whoami

### 8. Sign out — nulls session.userId (cookie itself stays)
POST http://localhost:3000/auth/signout
Content-Type: application/json

### 9. Create report — requires session cookie (AuthGuard)
POST http://localhost:3000/reports
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "make": "Toyota",
  "model": "Vitz",
  "year": 2014,
  "mileage": 100,
  "price": 14000
}

### 10. Approve report — requires admin (AdminGuard) -> 403 for non-admins
PATCH http://localhost:3000/reports/1
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "approved": true
}

### 11. Get report estimate — AVG of approved reports within +/-3 years, top 3 closest mileage
GET http://localhost:3000/reports?make=Toyota&model=Vitz&year=2014&mileage=100
